The messages shown are both from the panic() function.

> That's odd - when trying for Most Unique Deaths I killed myself by a
> potion of burning oil in the following ways with no problems.
> 
> * Drink it (message "killed by a burning potion of oil")
> * Throw it up in the air while nearly dead (message "killed by a
>   thrown potion")
> * Throw it against the wall so that it explodes (message "caught
>   herself in her own burning oil")
> * Possibly also repeat the above with flammable items in inventory
>   (message e.g. "killed by a boiling potion").

My guess would have been that the handling of burning potions of
oil are not coded correctly so that the game got in disorder (see
bug C343-52, that mentions the possibility of "odd game behavior").
Such behaviour is often only observable in an advanced game, if the
buggy code interacts with or affects other code; so it might be hard
to reproduce.

